[1] LL identity for the static O(G) harmonic metric (G=c=1); runtime so far 0.5 s
    16 pi (-g) t_LL^{00}: O(e) part = 0 ; O(e^2) part = -14*(Derivative(U(x, y, z), x)**2 + Derivative(U(x, y, z), y)**2 + Derivative(U(x, y, z), z)**2)
    16 pi (-g) t_LL^{11}: O(e) part = 0 ; O(e^2) part = 2*(Derivative(U(x, y, z), x)**2 - Derivative(U(x, y, z), y)**2 - Derivative(U(x, y, z), z)**2)
    16 pi (-g) t_LL^{12}: O(e) part = 0 ; O(e^2) part = 4*Derivative(U(x, y, z), x)*Derivative(U(x, y, z), y)
    16 pi (-g) t_LL^{22}: O(e) part = 0 ; O(e^2) part = -2*(Derivative(U(x, y, z), x)**2 - Derivative(U(x, y, z), y)**2 + Derivative(U(x, y, z), z)**2)
    16 pi (-g) t_LL^{33}: O(e) part = 0 ; O(e^2) part = -2*(Derivative(U(x, y, z), x)**2 + Derivative(U(x, y, z), y)**2 - Derivative(U(x, y, z), z)**2)
    => (-g) t_LL^{00} = -14 |grad U|^2 / (16 pi)  = -(7/8pi)|grad U|^2 ?  True
    => (-g) t_LL^{kk} = -2 |grad U|^2 / (16 pi)  = -(1/8pi)|grad U|^2 ?  True
    => (-g) t_LL^{xy} = 4 dxU dyU / (16 pi) = (1/4pi) dxU dyU ?  True
    (static t_H^{ab} is O(U^3): h^{0j}=0, h^{jk}=O(U^2); proved in report)

[2] O(M^2) harmonic point mass from tau = Lambda (outside the source), gothic -> g00
    h2^{00} = 7*M**2/r**2 ; h2^{kk} = M**2/r**2  (particular solutions; 1/r homogeneous parts = mass renormalisation)
    g00 to O(M^2) = -2*M**2/r**2 + 2*M/r - 1
    => beta = 1 (GR: 1)
    harmonic Schwarzschild comparator g00 = -2*M**2/r**2 + 2*M/r - 1
    aside: gothic metric LINEAR in records (Lambda = 0): g00 = -6*M**2/r**2 + 2*M/r - 1 -> beta = 3 ; metric-linear L0 (R16-14): beta = 0
    (perihelion factor (2+2gamma-beta)/3: beta=3 -> 1/3, beta=0 -> 4/3, beta=1 -> 1)
    runtime 0.8 s
